The fix: add `__or__` and `__ior__` to Headers/MutableHeaders in starlette/datastructures.py. The actual merged PR (encode/starlette#1241) added `__or__` to Headers and `__ior__` to MutableHeaders.

Actual implementation in starlette:

```python
class Headers(typing.Mapping[str, str]):
    def __or__(self, other: typing.Mapping[str, str]) -> "Headers":
        if not isinstance(other, typing.Mapping):
            raise TypeError(f"Expected a mapping but got {type(other)}.")
        new = dict(self.items())
        new.update(other)
        return Headers(new)


class MutableHeaders(Headers):
    def __ior__(self, other: typing.Mapping[str, str]) -> "MutableHeaders":
        if not isinstance(other, typing.Mapping):
            raise TypeError(f"Expected a mapping but got {type(other)}.")
        self.update(other)
        return self
```

